@page "/design"
@layout PgmStudio.Client.Layout.StudioLayout
@inject IJSRuntime JS

@* Living UI reference — verbatim port of studio/templates/design.html (the design system
   showcase). Uses tokens/components/editor/design CSS. *@

<StudioShell Bare="true">
  <Bar>
    <Topbar HomeHref="/" HomeLabel="Studio" HomeTitle="Back to dashboard">
      <Crumbs><Crumb>UI Reference</Crumb></Crumbs>
      <Right>
        <span class="ds-file-list">tokens.css · components.css · editor.css</span>
      </Right>
    </Topbar>
  </Bar>
  <ChildContent>

<div id="ds-layout">
  <nav id="ds-nav" aria-label="UI reference sections">
    <div class="ds-nav-group">Reference</div>
    <a href="#foundations">Foundations</a>
    <a href="#panels">Panel anatomy</a>
    <a href="#content">Panel content</a>
    <a href="#workspaces">Workspaces</a>
    <a href="#canvas">Canvas</a>
    <a href="#states">States</a>
    <a href="#suggestion">Smart suggestion</a>
    <a href="#cards">Cards &amp; navigation</a>
    <a href="#rules">Usage rules</a>
  </nav>

  <main id="ds-main">
    <header class="ds-intro">
      <p class="ds-kicker">Production-backed examples</p>
      <h1>Studio UI Reference</h1>
      <p>
        These examples use the same classes and nesting as Dashboard, Editor, and
        Sketch. Copy the structure, keep IDs as JavaScript handles, and add new
        component CSS only when no reference here fits.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="ds-section" id="foundations">
      <div class="ds-section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="ds-kicker">01</p>
          <h2>Foundations</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Use tokens for every repeated color, spacing, radius, shadow, and transition.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="ds-subsection">
        <h3>Surfaces and text</h3>
        <div class="ds-swatches">
          <div class="ds-swatch"><span class="ds-swatch-chip ds-bg-base"></span><code>--bg-base</code><small>Page background</small></div>
          <div class="ds-swatch"><span class="ds-swatch-chip ds-bg-panel"></span><code>--bg-panel</code><small>Shell and panels</small></div>
          <div class="ds-swatch"><span class="ds-swatch-chip ds-bg-deep"></span><code>--bg-deep</code><small>Recessed surface</small></div>
          <div class="ds-swatch"><span class="ds-swatch-chip ds-bg-canvas"></span><code>--bg-canvas</code><small>Map viewport</small></div>
          <div class="ds-swatch"><span class="ds-swatch-chip ds-bg-selected"></span><code>--bg-selected</code><small>Selection</small></div>
          <div class="ds-swatch"><span class="ds-swatch-chip ds-text-muted"></span><code>--text-muted</code><small>Quietest text</small></div>
          <div class="ds-swatch"><span class="ds-swatch-chip ds-text-primary"></span><code>--text-primary</code><small>Body text</small></div>
          <div class="ds-swatch"><span class="ds-swatch-chip ds-text-strong"></span><code>--text-strong</code><small>Headings / active</small></div>
          <div class="ds-swatch"><span class="ds-swatch-chip ds-accent"></span><code>--accent</code><small>Focus and primary</small></div>
          <div class="ds-swatch"><span class="ds-swatch-chip ds-error"></span><code>--color-error</code><small>Destructive/error</small></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="ds-subsection">
        <h3>Theming</h3>
        <p class="ds-theming-note">
          Two themes share one token set. Dark is the default; <code>&lt;html data-theme="light"&gt;</code>
          — toggled by the sun / moon button in the top bar — overrides only the <em>colour</em> tokens,
          while spacing, radii, type, and motion are shared. Toggle the theme to preview the swatches above
          live. The fixed game palettes (chat, dye, team, wool, and block-overlay colours) live outside CSS,
          so they stay the same in both themes.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="ds-subsection">
        <h3>Spacing rhythm</h3>
        <div class="ds-spacing">
          <div><span class="ds-space ds-space-1"></span><code>--space-1</code><small>4px</small></div>
          <div><span class="ds-space ds-space-2"></span><code>--space-2</code><small>8px</small></div>
          <div><span class="ds-space ds-space-3"></span><code>--space-3</code><small>12px</small></div>
          <div><span class="ds-space ds-space-4"></span><code>--space-4</code><small>16px</small></div>
          <div><span class="ds-space ds-space-5"></span><code>--space-5</code><small>20px</small></div>
          <div><span class="ds-space ds-space-6"></span><code>--space-6</code><small>24px</small></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ds-section" id="panels">
      <div class="ds-section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="ds-kicker">02</p>
          <h2>Panel anatomy</h2>
        </div>
        <p>A panel is a stack of sections. Each section has a header, body, and optional footer.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="ds-example-grid">
        <article class="ds-example">
          <div class="ds-example-label">Left sidebar form</div>
          <div class="ds-panel-frame">
            <div class="workspace-scroll">
              <Section Title="Map Identity">
                <ChildContent>
                  <div class="section-body">
                    <Field Label="Map Name" Required For="ds-map-name">
                      <input id="ds-map-name" class="field-input" value="Annealing V"/>
                    </Field>
                    <div class="field-row">
                      <Field Label="Version" For="ds-version">
                        <input id="ds-version" class="field-input" value="1.0.0"/>
                      </Field>
                      <Field Label="Mode" For="ds-mode" Class="field--compact">
                        <input id="ds-mode" class="field-input" value="ctw" disabled/>
                      </Field>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </ChildContent>
                <Footer>
                  <Button Variant="primary">Save changes</Button>
                  <span class="panel-save-status">Saved</span>
                </Footer>
              </Section>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="ds-example">
          <div class="ds-example-label">Right inspector</div>
          <div class="ds-panel-frame">
            <div class="workspace-scroll">
              <div class="panel-stack">
                <Section FooterClass="section-footer--separated">
                  <Header>
                    <DetailHeader Icon="cylinder" IconMuted Mono Label="red-spawn">
                      <Badge Kind="neutral">Cylinder</Badge>
                    </DetailHeader>
                  </Header>
                  <ChildContent>
                    <div class="section-body">
                      <Field Label="Base">
                        <div class="ctrl-row">
                          <CoordField Prefix="X" Value="48.5" />
                          <CoordField Prefix="Y" Value="9" />
                          <CoordField Prefix="Z" Value="-187" />
                        </div>
                      </Field>
                      <Field Label="Dimensions">
                        <div class="ctrl-row">
                          <CoordField Prefix="R" Value="0.5" />
                          <CoordField Prefix="H" Value="2" />
                        </div>
                      </Field>
                    </div>
                  </ChildContent>
                  <Footer>
                    <Button Variant="danger" Fill>Delete region</Button>
                  </Footer>
                </Section>
                <Section Title="Spawn Assignment">
                  <Field Label="Team">
                    <select class="field-input"><option>Red</option></select>
                  </Field>
                </Section>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ds-section" id="content">
      <div class="ds-section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="ds-kicker">03</p>
          <h2>Panel content</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Use explicit wrappers for repeated content so spacing belongs to the collection.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="ds-example-grid">
        <article class="ds-example">
          <div class="ds-example-label">Field row</div>
          <div class="ds-panel-frame">
            <div class="workspace-scroll">
              <Section Title="Map Version">
                <div class="field-row">
                  <Field Label="Version" For="ds-version-major">
                    <input id="ds-version-major" class="field-input" value="1.0.0"/>
                  </Field>
                  <Field Label="Mode" For="ds-version-mode" Class="field--compact">
                    <input id="ds-version-mode" class="field-input" value="ctw" disabled/>
                  </Field>
                </div>
              </Section>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="ds-example">
          <div class="ds-example-label">Panel list</div>
          <div class="ds-panel-frame">
            <div class="workspace-scroll">
              <Section Title="Teams">
                <Actions><Button>+ Add Team</Button></Actions>
                <ChildContent>
                  <div class="panel-list">
                    <ListRow Selected><span class="list-swatch ds-team-red"></span><span class="list-label">Red</span><Badge Kind="success">Ready</Badge></ListRow>
                    <ListRow><span class="list-swatch ds-team-blue"></span><span class="list-label">Blue</span><span class="list-tag">20 players</span></ListRow>
                    <ListRow Compact><span class="geo-type-icon"><i data-lucide="cylinder"></i></span><span class="list-label list-label--mono">red-spawn</span><span class="list-tag">Red</span></ListRow>
                    <ListRow>
                      <ChildContent><span class="list-label list-label--mono">drawn-map</span><span class="list-label">A row with its own action</span></ChildContent>
                      <Trailing><Button Icon="external-link">Open elsewhere</Button></Trailing>
                    </ListRow>
                  </div>
                </ChildContent>
              </Section>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="ds-example">
          <div class="ds-example-label">Author list</div>
          <div class="ds-panel-frame">
            <div class="workspace-scroll">
              <Section Title="Authors" Required>
                <Actions><Button>+ Add</Button></Actions>
                <ChildContent>
                  <div class="author-list">
                    <div class="author-row">
                      <span class="author-avatar"></span>
                      <input class="field-input author-name" value="fakejustcupcakes"/>
                      <input class="field-input author-contribution" placeholder="Contribution (optional)"/>
                      <button class="btn-remove" title="Remove"><i data-lucide="x"></i></button>
                    </div>
                    <div class="author-row">
                      <span class="author-avatar"></span>
                      <input class="field-input author-name" value="killAce"/>
                      <input class="field-input author-contribution" value="Terrain"/>
                      <button class="btn-remove" title="Remove"><i data-lucide="x"></i></button>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </ChildContent>
              </Section>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="ds-example">
          <div class="ds-example-label">Control list</div>
          <div class="ds-panel-frame">
            <div class="workspace-scroll">
              <Section Title="Overlays">
                <div class="control-list">
                  <label class="check-row"><input type="checkbox" checked/>Mirror preview</label>
                  <label class="check-row"><input type="checkbox"/>Shapes overlay</label>
                  <label class="check-row"><input type="checkbox" checked/>Chunk grid</label>
                </div>
              </Section>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="ds-example">
          <div class="ds-example-label">Region tree</div>
          <div class="ds-panel-frame">
            <div class="workspace-scroll">
              <Section Title="Wool Regions">
                <div class="region-tree">
                  <div class="geo-row geo-row--selected">
                    <span class="geo-indent">
                      <button class="collapse-btn" title="Collapse"><i data-lucide="chevron-down"></i></button>
                    </span>
                    <span class="geo-type-icon"><i data-lucide="combine"></i></span>
                    <span class="geo-label">purple-wool-room</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="geo-row geo-row--selected-child">
                    <span class="geo-indent"><span class="indent-pipe"></span></span>
                    <span class="geo-type-icon"><i data-lucide="box"></i></span>
                    <span class="geo-label">purple-wool-bounds</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="geo-row">
                    <span class="geo-indent"></span>
                    <span class="geo-type-icon"><i data-lucide="cylinder"></i></span>
                    <span class="geo-label">orange-wool-room</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </Section>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ds-section" id="workspaces">
      <div class="ds-section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="ds-kicker">04</p>
          <h2>Workspaces</h2>
        </div>
        <p>The sidebar and inspector share the same panel construction. Handles sit directly beside resizable panels.</p>
      </div>

      <article class="ds-example">
        <div class="ds-example-label">Three-column activity workspace</div>
        <div class="ds-workspace-frame">
          <Workspace>
            <Sidebar>
              <Section Title="Islands">
                <div class="panel-list">
                  <ListRow Selected><span class="geo-type-icon"><i data-lucide="layers"></i></span><span class="list-label">Center</span></ListRow>
                  <ListRow><span class="geo-type-icon"><i data-lucide="layers"></i></span><span class="list-label">Team island</span></ListRow>
                </div>
              </Section>
            </Sidebar>
            <div class="sidebar-handle"></div>
            <div class="workspace-canvas">
              <div class="canvas-surface ds-canvas-sample">
                <span class="ds-axis ds-axis-x"></span>
                <span class="ds-axis ds-axis-z"></span>
                <span class="ds-region-sample"></span>
              </div>
              <CanvasReadout ZoomText="100%"><span class="canvas-readout-item">X 128 Z -64</span></CanvasReadout>
              <CanvasLayerBar>
                <LayerChip Icon="box" Active>Blocks</LayerChip>
                <CanvasRoundButton Icon="scan" Title="Fit" />
              </CanvasLayerBar>
              <CanvasDock>
                <DockGroup>
                  <DockButton Icon="mouse-pointer-2" Title="Select" Active />
                  <DockButton Icon="hand" Title="Move" />
                </DockGroup>
                <DockGroup Accent="var(--canvas-add-fill)">
                  <DockModeButton>Build</DockModeButton>
                  <DockButton Icon="rectangle-horizontal" Title="Rectangle" Active />
                </DockGroup>
              </CanvasDock>
            </div>
            <div class="sidebar-handle"></div>
            <Inspector>
              <Section>
                <Header>
                  <DetailHeader Icon="rectangle-horizontal" IconMuted Label="Team island">
                    <Badge Kind="neutral">Rectangle</Badge>
                  </DetailHeader>
                </Header>
                <ChildContent>
                  <Field Label="Operation"><Badge Kind="success">Add</Badge></Field>
                </ChildContent>
              </Section>
            </Inspector>
          </Workspace>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="ds-section" id="canvas">
      <div class="ds-section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="ds-kicker">05</p>
          <h2>Canvas chrome</h2>
        </div>
        <p>A canvas control floats on the map, placed by what it is — never in a bar above it.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="ds-theming-note">Three positions, and each answers one question. <strong>Top-left</strong>
         is what the canvas <em>is</em> — cursor position, the live size of what is being drawn or measured,
         zoom (<code>CanvasReadout</code>). It is read-only and pointer-transparent, so a drag that crosses
         it never stalls, and an item with nothing to report collapses. <strong>Top-right</strong> is what
         the canvas <em>shows</em> (<code>CanvasLayerBar</code>): the layer chips, then the view actions that
         only move the camera (<code>CanvasRoundButton</code> — fit, rotate), then <code>ViewModeToggle</code>
         in the very corner, outermost because it decides what every other control in the row means.
         <strong>Bottom-centre</strong> is what the pointer <em>does</em> (<code>CanvasDock</code>), where
         the pointer already is.</p>
      <div class="ds-canvas-bar-example ds-canvas-sample">
        <span class="ds-axis ds-axis-x"></span>
        <span class="ds-axis ds-axis-z"></span>
        <CanvasReadout ZoomText="100%"><span class="canvas-readout-item">X 128 Z -64</span><span class="canvas-readout-item canvas-readout-item--size">48 × 32</span></CanvasReadout>
        <CanvasLayerBar>
          <LayerChip Icon="grid" Active>Chunks</LayerChip>
          <LayerChip Icon="box">Blocks</LayerChip>
          <CanvasRoundButton Icon="scan" Title="Fit the working bounds" />
          <ViewModeToggle Title="Isometric height preview" />
        </CanvasLayerBar>
        <CanvasDock>
          <DockGroup>
            <DockButton Icon="mouse-pointer-2" Title="Select" Active />
            <DockButton Icon="hand" Title="Move" />
          </DockGroup>
          <DockGroup Accent="var(--canvas-add-fill)">
            <DockModeButton>Build</DockModeButton>
            <DockButton Icon="rectangle-horizontal" Title="Rectangle" Active />
            <DockButton Icon="pentagon" Title="Polygon" />
            <DockButton Icon="lasso" Title="Lasso" />
          </DockGroup>
          <DockGroup>
            <DockButton Icon="ruler" Title="Measure" />
            <DockButton Icon="scissors" Title="Split" />
          </DockGroup>
        </CanvasDock>
      </div>

      <div class="ds-subsection" style="margin-top:var(--space-5)">
        <h3>Dock groups</h3>
        <p class="ds-theming-note">The dock holds <code>DockGroup</code>s, never loose buttons: a group is
           one question the tool answers, and the gaps between them are the only grouping a row of equal
           glyphs can carry. A group may carry an <strong>accent</strong> — the colour of the mode it is
           armed in — which reaches every control inside it as <code>--dock-accent</code>, so a
           <code>DockModeButton</code>'s word and the shape buttons beside it state the same thing at once
           and an armed carve cannot be read as an armed build. A family with too many options to lay out
           collapses into a <code>DockFlyoutGroup</code>: the option in hand plus a chevron, the rest in a
           flyout that opens upward, and picking one promotes it into the slot.</p>
        <div class="ds-state-row">
          <DockGroup Accent="var(--canvas-sub-fill)">
            <DockModeButton Pressed>Carve</DockModeButton>
            <DockButton Icon="rectangle-horizontal" Title="Rectangle" Active />
            <DockButton Icon="pentagon" Title="Polygon" />
          </DockGroup>
          <DockGroup>
            <DockButton Swatch="#3fae74" Title="Wool room" Active />
            <DockButton SwatchClass="canvas-dock-swatch--build" Title="Build zone" />
            <DockButton Swatch="#4ea3d8" SwatchClass="canvas-dock-swatch--box" Title="Hub box" />
          </DockGroup>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="ds-subsection" style="margin-top:var(--space-5)">
        <h3>Flow bar (wizard steps)</h3>
        <p class="ds-theming-note">A clean wizard step strip for guided multi-step phases — a
           left-aligned <strong>phase-identity cluster</strong> (<code>flow-bar-phase</code>: the current
           phase's icon + name), then flat-text step labels with an accent underline on the active one
           (a status icon on completed ones is deferred to ND4, where step status gets meaning), then
           Back/Next on the right (Back disabled at the first step). It is its <strong>own strip</strong>
           (<code>FlowBar</code>) above the workspace — never on the canvas, whose chrome is the readout,
           layer bar and dock above. Used by the Configure wizard and Edit's stepped phases (Setup, Build).</p>
        <FlowBar PhaseIcon="goal" PhaseTitle="Wools" Steps="@(new[] { "Colours", "Spawn & room", "Monuments" })"
                 CurrentStep="1" BackEnabled="true" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ds-section" id="states">
      <div class="ds-section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="ds-kicker">06</p>
          <h2>Actions and states</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Use one vocabulary for actions, status, empty content, validation, and confidence meters.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ds-state-row">
        <Button>Secondary</Button>
        <Button Variant="primary">Primary</Button>
        <Button Variant="warn">Pending</Button>
        <Button Variant="danger">Delete</Button>
        <Badge Kind="success">Ready</Badge>
        <Badge Kind="warning">Review</Badge>
        <Badge Kind="error">Invalid</Badge>
        <Badge Kind="neutral">Cylinder</Badge>
        <Badge Kind="dim">Optional</Badge>
      </div>
      <div class="ds-state-grid">
        <div class="panel-warning">The selected region overlaps the map boundary.</div>
        <div class="ds-empty-sample"><p class="panel-empty-msg">Select a team or region to inspect.</p></div>
        <Field Label="ID" Error='Region ID "spawn-red" is already in use.'>
          <input class="field-input field-input--error" value="spawn-red"/>
        </Field>
      </div>
      @* Meter — thin confidence/score bar (track + .meter-fill; width inline, colour band by modifier).
         Used for ranked monument suggestions. *@
      <div class="ds-state-grid" style="margin-top:var(--space-4)">
        <Field Label="Confidence · high"><LabelHint>0.90</LabelHint><ChildContent><div class="meter"><div class="meter-fill" style="width:90%"></div></div></ChildContent></Field>
        <Field Label="Confidence · mid"><LabelHint>0.55</LabelHint><ChildContent><div class="meter"><div class="meter-fill meter-fill--mid" style="width:55%"></div></div></ChildContent></Field>
        <Field Label="Confidence · low"><LabelHint>0.25</LabelHint><ChildContent><div class="meter"><div class="meter-fill meter-fill--low" style="width:25%"></div></div></ChildContent></Field>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ds-section" id="suggestion">
      <div class="ds-section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="ds-kicker">07</p>
          <h2>Smart suggestion</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Sparkle-headed callout for studio-inferred actions (symmetry → teams, wiring, wools).
           Reusable <code>&lt;SmartSuggestion&gt;</code> — header (icon + title + badge), body, accept/dismiss.
           The suggested-team preview is always a 2-column grid (2 teams → one row, 4 → two).</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ds-sug-sample">
        <SmartSuggestion Header="Smart Suggestion" Badge="rot 90" AcceptLabel="Create 4 teams" RejectLabel="Dismiss">
          <p class="smart-suggestion__text">90° rotational symmetry suggests four teams.</p>
          <div class="smart-suggestion-teams">
            <div class="smart-suggestion-team"><span class="list-swatch list-swatch--sm" style="background:#FF5555"></span>Red Team</div>
            <div class="smart-suggestion-team"><span class="list-swatch list-swatch--sm" style="background:#5555FF"></span>Blue Team</div>
            <div class="smart-suggestion-team"><span class="list-swatch list-swatch--sm" style="background:#55FF55"></span>Green Team</div>
            <div class="smart-suggestion-team"><span class="list-swatch list-swatch--sm" style="background:#FFFF55"></span>Yellow Team</div>
          </div>
        </SmartSuggestion>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ds-section" id="cards">
      <div class="ds-section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="ds-kicker">08</p>
          <h2>Cards &amp; navigation</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Entry surfaces. <code>.card-grid</code> of <code>.card</code> — as a navigable
           <code>.card--action</code> with a <code>.card-foot</code> (count + go affordance), and the
           landing pattern that fans out to the staged dashboard. List rows gain a hover
           <code>.list-go</code> arrow when they navigate.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-4)">
        <a class="card card--action" href="#cards">
          <div class="card-head">
            <span class="card-icon"><i data-lucide="pencil-ruler"></i></span>
            <span class="card-title">Sketch</span>
          </div>
          <p class="card-desc">Draw a new map's islands from nothing — shapes, symmetry and mirror.</p>
          <span class="card-foot">
            <span class="card-foot-count">3 drafts</span>
            <span class="card-foot-go">Browse <i data-lucide="arrow-right"></i></span>
          </span>
        </a>
        <a class="card card--action" href="#cards">
          <div class="card-head">
            <span class="card-icon"><i data-lucide="settings-2"></i></span>
            <span class="card-title">Configure</span>
          </div>
          <p class="card-desc">Turn a terrain-only world into a playable <code>map.xml</code>.</p>
          <span class="card-foot">
            <span class="card-foot-count">7 in progress</span>
            <span class="card-foot-go">Browse <i data-lucide="arrow-right"></i></span>
          </span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div style="max-width: 420px; background: var(--bg-panel); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-md); padding: var(--space-3)">
        <div class="panel-list">
          <ListRow Href="#cards">
            <span class="list-label list-label--mono">annealing_iv</span>
